# Dual git (this repo)

Remotes:

- `origin` → `https://github.com/ahmadubuntu/wso2_relateds.git`
- `azure` → `https://azure.charisma.tech/DataPlatform/DataPlatform/_git/wso2_relateds`

Auth for Azure: env **`AZDO_PAT_DATAPLATFORM`** only (not `AZDO_PAT`).

Every push in this repo must update **both** remotes in the same turn:

```bash
AUTH_HEADER="AUTHORIZATION: Basic $(printf ':%s' "$AZDO_PAT_DATAPLATFORM" | base64 -w0)"
git push -u origin HEAD
git -c credential.helper= -c http.extraHeader="$AUTH_HEADER" push -u azure HEAD
# when tags changed:
git push origin --tags
git -c credential.helper= -c http.extraHeader="$AUTH_HEADER" push azure --tags
git branch --set-upstream-to=origin/<branch> <branch>
```

Never embed the PAT in the remote URL. Never dump the token.
